Feature: Primary button and text link
  The paywall purchase button and its log-in link: one Core component, platform values kept as shipped (DEC-07, DEC-22, DEC-24).

  Rule: The primary button looks the same in every market except its fill

    Scenario Outline: Enabled primary button on <platform>
      Given the <platform> app for any market
      When a primary button is enabled
      Then its fill is the market's action color
      And its label is white, <label>
      And it is <height> tall with corner radius <radius>
      And it has <border>

      Examples:
        | platform | label                               | height | radius | border                            |
        | iOS      | Open Sans Bold 14, always uppercase | 45 pt  | 8 pt   | a 0.7 pt border in the fill color |
        | Android  | Roboto Medium 14sp, uppercase       | 60 dp  | 0 dp   | no border                         |

    Scenario Outline: Pressed primary button on <platform>
      Given an enabled primary button in the <platform> app
      When the reader presses it
      Then <feedback>
      And no custom pressed color is used

      Examples:
        | platform | feedback                                                   |
        | iOS      | the title fades and the fill stays the same (UIKit system) |
        | Android  | the Material ripple plays over the fill                    |

    Scenario: Disabled primary button
      Given a primary button is disabled
      Then its fill is #c1c8cb and its label is #767676 (2.68:1)
      And it does not respond to taps
      # Disabled controls are exempt from WCAG 1.4.3. Android ships this on Continue; new on iOS.

    Scenario Outline: Purchase in progress on <platform>
      Given the reader tapped the primary button
      When the purchase is in progress
      Then the button shows no spinner of its own
      And <loading> covers the screen

      Examples:
        | platform | loading                       |
        | iOS      | a full-screen overlay         |
        | Android  | a full-screen progress dialog |

